    <div class="container">
        <span class="section-label">Service</span>
        <h1>Advisory &amp; Board Roles</h1>
        <p>An independent technical voice at the table where the real calls get made.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="service-detail fade-in">
            <h2>Service Overview</h2>
            <p>Boards, executive teams, and founders make big technical bets with incomplete information. I serve as an independent technical advisor to those rooms&mdash;challenging the comfortable assumption, pressure-testing the roadmap, and surfacing the risks nobody inside wants to name. My job isn&rsquo;t to be right more often than your team. It&rsquo;s to make sure the conversation is honest, the trade-offs are visible, and the decision gets made on the best available picture of reality.</p>

            <h2>Who This Is For</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Founders and CEOs without a technical co-founder who need a trusted second opinion</li>
                <li>Boards of Series A&ndash;C companies evaluating platform bets, acquisitions, or CTO performance</li>
                <li>Private-equity and portfolio operators assessing technology risk across multiple holdings</li>
                <li>CTOs and VPs of Engineering who want a sounding board their own team can&rsquo;t provide</li>
                <li>Nonprofit and mission-driven organizations facing a consequential tech modernization</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>How I Contribute</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Technical advisory for executive teams and boards of directors</li>
                <li>Platform strategy, technology roadmap review, and reality-checking of in-flight plans</li>
                <li>Risk assessment for major technical investments, vendor choices, and acquisitions</li>
                <li>Innovation strategy and emerging-technology evaluation with a clear separation of signal from hype</li>
                <li>Mentorship for CTOs, VPs of Engineering, and senior technical leaders</li>
                <li>Independent input during CEO/CTO performance reviews and succession conversations</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Engagement Models</h2>
            <p><strong>Board Advisor</strong> &ndash; Attend quarterly board meetings as the technical voice, with prep and follow-up time. Annual commitment.</p>
            <p><strong>Executive Advisor</strong> &ndash; A standing monthly call plus async availability for the CEO, CTO, or founding team. Renewed quarterly.</p>
            <p><strong>Portfolio Advisor</strong> &ndash; A retained technical advisor across several PE- or VC-backed companies, with structured check-ins and ad hoc deep-dives.</p>

            <h2>What You Get</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>An independent technical perspective with no internal politics and no incentive to flatter</li>
                <li>Pre-meeting prep notes and post-meeting written follow-ups, so insights don&rsquo;t evaporate</li>
                <li>Direct access between meetings when something urgent comes up</li>
                <li>Strict NDA, conflict-free engagements, and a capped number of active advisory seats</li>
                <li>A partner who reads the deck before the meeting&mdash;and says so when it doesn&rsquo;t hold up</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Why Work With Me</h2>
            <p><strong>Hands Still on the Keyboard</strong> &ndash; I&rsquo;m not a former practitioner. Architecture and engagements keep my advice grounded in what&rsquo;s actually shipping today.</p>
            <p><strong>Independence Over Access</strong> &ndash; I limit the number of concurrent advisory roles I take on, so each one gets real attention and an honest voice.</p>
            <p><strong>Written, Not Just Spoken</strong> &ndash; You get follow-up notes after every meeting. The guidance survives the next quarter, not just the hour.</p>

            <div class="service-cta">
                <h3>Looking for an independent technical voice at the table?</h3>
                <p>Let&rsquo;s talk about the decisions on your horizon and whether I&rsquo;m the right fit.</p>
                <a href="/Contact" class="btn btn-primary">Start the Conversation <span class="btn-arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>

            <div class="service-nav">
                <a href="/Services/DevRel">&larr; Developer Relations</a>
                <a href="/Services/FractionalArchitect">Fractional Architect &rarr;</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
